From dbc09a32f51793b4e3e42f3d2a1547aef1af4ee2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karan Shukla <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:20:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] backends/drm: send FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS for composited frames

Fills the property from the damage of the frame the compositor rendered, so
the kernel can do selective fetch / selective update instead of treating
every commit as fully damaged. Falls back to the old value 0 (no clips)
whenever the damage is not known: direct scanout, the first frame after
it, cursor and software layers, scaled or transformed planes.

Damage that was rendered but not submitted accumulates, and the commit
thread unions it when it merges commits so a skipped frame is not lost.
